WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.406 --> 00:00:03.587
Unit two. API and Data Basics!

2
00:00:04.518 --> 00:00:08.959
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:12.429
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:16.249
Today we learn about API and Data Basics. Let's go!

5
00:00:17.423 --> 00:00:21.381
API. Say it with me. API!

6
00:00:24.878 --> 00:00:29.078
JSON. Say it with me. JSON!

7
00:00:32.512 --> 00:00:36.212
Endpoint. Say it with me. Endpoint!

8
00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:43.415
Request. Say it with me. Request!

9
00:00:46.921 --> 00:00:51.087
Response. Say it with me. Response!

10
00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:59.500
Authentication key. Say it with me. Authentication key!

11
00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.780
Rate limit. Say it with me. Rate limit!

12
00:01:10.266 --> 00:01:14.750
Data format. Say it with me. Data format!

13
00:01:18.274 --> 00:01:34.484
An API lets one program talk to another, often exchanging data in JSON format. Sending a request to an endpoint returns a response, sometimes requiring an authentication key. A rate limit controls how often a program can make a request.

14
00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:38.085
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:38.811 --> 00:01:44.228
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:44.278 --> 00:01:45.428
Endpoint!

17
00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:51.655
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:51.705 --> 00:01:52.855
Rate limit!

19
00:01:53.753 --> 00:02:01.235
Did you know? When a weather app shows you the forecast, it's usually using an API to fetch that data from a weather service!

20
00:02:01.285 --> 00:02:03.449
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:04.882 --> 00:02:13.640
Think and answer. Can you think of an app that probably uses an API to work?

22
00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:14.840
Great answer!

23
00:02:15.976 --> 00:02:21.030
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.056
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

